   $q$How do the two texts differ in what they suggest reading can do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 suggests books can renew a reader's view of home, while Text 2 celebrates books as a way to travel far from home.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both texts suggest that reading makes rural life seem dull and that readers should leave.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"Text 1 celebrates books only as escape from home, while Text 2 suggests books teach readers to love their own valley.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both texts suggest that books matter less than the friendships formed at the stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 suggests books can renew a reader's view of home, while Text 2 celebrates books as a way to travel far from home.$q$, $q$Ruthanne decides her job is also to "send them home again, seeing it for the first time," while the poem ends with Thursday carrying the speaker "from home." Swapping these ideas confuses the texts.$q$, 'draft', '89168ac2-e95f-5718-b890-fee0b30602bf')
