   $q$How does the van in Text 1 function compared with the stilled stopwatch in Text 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The van is a tempting chance to quit that Femi must refuse, while the stilled stopwatch shows that official measurement has ended though the race goes on.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both objects show that the city wants slow runners to keep going and will wait for every one of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The van carries the winner to the finish line, while the stopwatch records Femi's final time for the newspaper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The van stands for official measurement ending, while the stopwatch is a tempting chance for the runner to quit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The van is a tempting chance to quit that Femi must refuse, while the stilled stopwatch shows that official measurement has ended though the race goes on.$q$, $q$Femi looks at the open van "for a long moment" before running on, and the poem's stopwatch "has been stilled" even as the speaker waits for the last runner. The poem says no one will print the runner's time, so the stopwatch records nothing.$q$, 'draft', '0ffe9028-d76f-5540-8d17-2fe7e203e06b')
